		{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the SDK give me access to?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You get access to the device throught the SDK. This means that the camera(s), microphone and other sensor data are yours to tap into. Build your own UI on the heads-up display, etc. What you build with it, and how, is entirely up to you: it's your app, on-device, running your own logic."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the SDK available for Android and iOS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, we have an SDK for each. Apps ship through the Play Store or App Store."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which glasses does it support, and is the G3 supported?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our SDK supports all our smart glasses, the G2, H1 and G3."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we get the SDK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Through the developer program. You receive credentials, sign an NDA and SDK agreement, and get access to the documentation and sample apps."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do we need any other apps from Iristick?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The SDK stands on its own, you do not need any other app from us to work with the SDK."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does it cost to start?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Developer Package: a development unit at 50% off (€1.137,50), three months of SDK access and a 30-minute onboarding Q&A. Continued access is €1,000 per year."}}]}
